      "created_at": "2012-04-15T19:13:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This question also applies to similar cards; Undaunted and Superhuman Durability.</p>\n<p>So, the cards state that whenever (Hero) would be dealt &gt;5 damage from a single source, reduce it by 2.</p>\n<p>Am I correct in saying here that this does not have to come from a single “attack”?  This didn’t really come up pre-RC, but now it actually comes up a lot:</p>\n<p>Spite:  On his turn with all his drug cards out DK=2 damage, Phyre=2 damage, basic attack=2 to all but lowest.   This adds up to 6 damage from a single source (Spite).   Does Shielding Winds activate?</p>\n<p>Plague Rat:   Vicious Onslaught deals 2 toxic damage and 2 melee damage.   If on advanced mode or with Plague Locus in play, 3+3 damage= 6 damage from one source (plague Rat)   but again,  over multiple “attacks”.</p>\n<p>Matriarch:  When you kill a lot of birds its quite possible thatt &gt;5 damage could be coming in to a hero from one source (matriarch) , especially if Huginn/Muninn are in play, increasing her damage.   Carrion Fields can create the same effect when destroying a lot of birds.</p>\n<p>Also, would this like a “per round”  kind of thing?   I’m assuming yes but I have really not much to base it off of.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:19.240Z",
